    <ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>&lt;div&gt;A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;On 7 November 2013, the Minister of Veteran Affairs introduced Bill C-11, An Act to amend the Public Service Employment Act (priority hiring for injured veterans) (Priority Hiring for Injured Veterans Act) in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Every year, many military members transition out of the Canadian Armed Forces. For those Canadian Armed Forces members who cannot deploy and meet the demands of operations, finding meaningful employment is a key factor in making a successful transition to civilian life.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Bill C-11 amends the Public Service Employment Act to establish a right of appointment, in priority to all other persons, for certain members of the Canadian Forces who are released for medical reasons that are attributable to service.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>
    <ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>&lt;div&gt;Le Service d'information et de recherche parlementaires de la Bibliothèque du Parlement rédige actuellement le résumé législatif de ce projet de loi. Entre-temps, le Service met à votre disposition le sommaire suivant. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Le 7 novembre 2013, le ministre des Anciens Combattants a déposé le projet de loi C-11, Loi modifiant la Loi sur l'emploi dans la fonction publique (priorité d'emploi aux anciens combattants blessés)  (Loi sur la priorité d'emploi aux anciens combattants blessés) à la Chambres des communes en première lecture.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Chaque année, de nombreux militaires quittent les Forces armées canadiennes. Les militaires qui ne peuvent plus être déployés et qui sont incapables d'effectuer les tâches propres à leur poste comptent beaucoup sur un emploi valorisant afin de réussir leur transition à la vie civile. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Le projet de loi C-11 modifie la Loi sur l'emploi dans la fonction publique afin d'établir le droit à une priorité de nomination absolue pour certains militaires libérés des Forces canadiennes pour des raisons médicales qui sont attribuables au service.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>
    <ShortLegislativeSummary>&lt;div&gt;A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;On 7 November 2013, the Minister of Veteran Affairs introduced Bill C-11, An Act to amend the Public Service Employment Act (priority hiring for injured veterans) (Priority Hiring for Injured Veterans Act) in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Every year, many military members transition out of the Canadian Armed Forces. For those Canadian Armed Forces members who cannot deploy and meet the demands of operations, finding meaningful employment is a key factor in making a successful transition to civilian life.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Bill C-11 amends the Public Service Employment Act to establish a right of appointment, in priority to all other persons, for certain members of the Canadian Forces who are released for medical reasons that are attributable to service.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummary>
